# The Three Crowns, 10-player normal, paladin:protection, style=dodge, fresh save.
# dodge is one of the two vocabulary styles (with wander) that have not yet been
# tried on this fight -- direction.md #7's melee/good/idle pulls all beeline at
# hud().boss (the one named body), which is sometimes the untouchable decoy, and
# spend the whole fight parked in its thirst radius. dodge never presses an
# ability and has no toward-boss term at all (only away-from-danger), so this
# checks whether a style with no reason to walk at the boss actually avoids the
# drain the beelining styles couldn't see, or parks in it anyway some other way.
open #b=crowns&s=10&h=0
targets
tap class:paladin:protection
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start
play dodge 90
bill
shot mid1
state
play dodge 90
bill
shot mid2
state
play dodge 90
bill
shot end
state
